70-a433-5de2-8209-ac0435d5fb1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493931 #edb/ref 1074 "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4-8\\text{i} \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4{\\text{i}}^{2}-8\\text{i} \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i}(4-2\\text{i}) \\\\ 1(4-2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(4-2\\text{i})[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(4-2\\text{i})v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=(4-2\\text{i})v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =4-2\\text{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493981 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "156e434a-b38e-5003-b3b2-3990ebd3f421" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493981 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186351251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494011 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186494042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494011 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "64c77246-92ab-5343-a010-84041f103bc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494011 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494015 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186493981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494015 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7665ea0d-01a8-57f6-bbbc-8dc06d46bcb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494015 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186493931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494019 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186494015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494019 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7bf20b01-76bc-543c-a0e8-b3bf2f4563c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494019 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186351199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494042 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186494019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494042 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b37de30-2d0f-54d1-9978-97a780796cdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494042 #edb/ref 106